Problem: Number of Closed Islands (LC 1254)

Pattern: DFS / Flood Fill

Approach:

1. Traverse every cell in the grid.
2. When an unvisited land cell (`0`) is found, call DFS.
3. If DFS goes outside the grid, return `true` because this alone does not determine whether the island is open.
4. If the cell contains water (`1`), return `true`.
5. Mark the land cell as visited by changing `0` to `1`.
6. If the land cell touches the boundary, mark the island as not closed.
7. Explore all four directions: up, down, left, and right.
8. Combine the results using `&&`. If any connected land cell touches the boundary, DFS returns `false`.
9. Increase the count only if DFS returns `true`.

Time Complexity: \\(O(m \times n)\\)

Space Complexity: \\(O(m \times n)\\) in the worst case due to the DFS recursion stack.